port names that are all strings. \"\n1632 |             f\"Got feature names with dtypes: {types}. An error will be raised \"\n1633 |             \"in 1.2.\",\n1634 |             FutureWarning,\n1635 |         )\n1636 |         return\n1637 | \n1638 |     # Only feature names of all strings are supported\n1639 |     if types[0] == \"str\":\n1640 |         return feature_names\n```\n\nFound function `sklearn/datasets/_base.py:load_diabetes`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n 911 | def load_diabetes(*, return_X_y=False, as_frame=False):\n 912 |     \"\"\"Load and return the diabetes dataset (regression).\n 913 | \n 914 |     ==============   ==================\n 915 |     Samples total    442\n 916 |     Dimensionality   10\n 917 |     Features         real, -.2 < x < .2\n 918 |     Targets          integer 25 - 346\n 919 |     ==============   ==================\n 920 | \n 921 |     .. note::\n 922 |        The meaning of each feature (i.e. `feature_names`) might be unclear\n 923 |        (especially for `ltg`) as the documentation of the original dataset is\n 924 |        not explicit. We provide information that seems correct in regard with\n 925 |        the scientific literature in this field of research.\n 926 | \n 927 |     Read more in the :ref:`User Guide <diabetes_dataset>`.\n 928 | \n 929 |     Parameters\n 930 |     ----------\n 931 |     return_X_y : bool, default=False.\n 932 |         If True, returns ``(data, target)`` instead of a Bunch object.\n 933 |         See below for more information about the `data` and `target` object.\n 934 | \n 935 |         .. versionadded:: 0.18\n 936 | \n 937 |     as_frame : bool, default=False\n 938 |         If True, the data is a pandas DataFrame including columns with\n 939 |         appropriate dtypes (numeric). The target is\n 940 |         a pandas DataFrame or Series depending on the number of target columns.\n 941 |         If `return_X_y` is True, then (`data`, `target`) will 