s/core/indexes/interval.py:IntervalIndex.left`.\nSource: Match found for entity name `left`.\n```\n846 | def left(self) -> Index:\n847 |         \"\"\"\n848 |         Return left bounds of the intervals in the IntervalIndex.\n849 | \n850 |         The left bounds of each interval in the IntervalIndex are\n851 |         returned as an Index. The datatype of the left bounds is the\n852 |         same as the datatype of the endpoints of the intervals.\n853 | \n854 |         Returns\n855 |         -------\n856 |         Index\n857 |             An Index containing the left bounds of the intervals.\n858 | \n859 |         See Also\n860 |         --------\n861 |         IntervalIndex.right : Return the right bounds of the intervals\n862 |             in the IntervalIndex.\n863 |         IntervalIndex.mid : Return the mid-point of the intervals in\n864 |             the IntervalIndex.\n865 |         IntervalIndex.length : Return the length of the intervals in\n866 |             the IntervalIndex.\n867 | \n868 |         Examples\n869 |         --------\n870 |         >>> iv_idx = pd.IntervalIndex.from_arrays([1, 2, 3], [4, 5, 6], closed=\"right\")\n871 |         >>> iv_idx.left\n872 |         Index([1, 2, 3], dtype='int64')\n873 | \n874 |         >>> iv_idx = pd.IntervalIndex.from_tuples(\n875 |         ...     [(1, 4), (2, 5), (3, 6)], closed=\"left\"\n876 |         ... )\n877 |         >>> iv_idx.left\n878 |         Index([1, 2, 3], dtype='int64')\n879 |         \"\"\"\n880 |         return Index(self._data.left, copy=False)\n```\n\n\n\n##Searching for term \"right\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound function `pandas/core/arrays/interval.py:IntervalArray.right`.\nSource: Match found for entity name `right`.\n```\n1270 | def right(self) -> Index:\n1271 |         \"\"\"\n1272 |         Return the right endpoints of each Interval in the IntervalArray as an Index.\n1273 | \n1274 |         This property extracts the right endpoints from each interval contained within\n1275 |       