ous search encountered an error. Let's try a different approach by focusing directly on the lines mentioned in the issue statement (234 and 235) and then searching for the functions `_evaluate` and `_evaluate_standard` that were mentioned in the supplemental context.\n\n<function=search_code_snippets>\n<parameter=line_nums>[234, 235]</parameter>\n<parameter=file_path_or_pattern>pandas/core/computation/expressions.py</parameter>\n", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "toolu_01", "name": "search_code_snippets", "content": "OBSERVATION:\n##Searching for term \"pandas/core/computation/expressions.py:line 234, 235\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound function `pandas/core/computation/expressions.py:evaluate`.\nSource: Retrieved code context including pandas/core/computation/expressions.py:line 234, 235.\n```\n227 | def evaluate(op, a, b, use_numexpr: bool = True):\n228 |     \"\"\"\n229 |     Evaluate and return the expression of the op on a and b.\n230 | \n231 |     Parameters\n232 |     ----------\n233 |     op : the actual operand\n234 |     a : left operand\n235 |     b : right operand\n236 |     use_numexpr : bool, default True\n237 |         Whether to try to use numexpr.\n238 |     \"\"\"\n239 |     op_str = _op_str_mapping[op]\n240 |     if op_str is not None:\n241 |         if use_numexpr:\n242 |             # error: \"None\" not callable\n243 |             return _evaluate(op, op_str, a, b)  # type: ignore[misc]\n244 |     return _evaluate_standard(op, op_str, a, b)\n```\n"}, {"content": "Based on the search results, the relevant functions and lines are clearly identified. Let's now focus on the `_evaluate` and `_evaluate_standard` functions for more context.\n\n<function=search_code_snippets>\n<parameter=search_terms>[\"_evaluate\", \"_evaluate_standard\"]</parameter>\n<parameter=file_path_or_pattern>pandas/core/computation/expressions.py</parameter>\n Protective measure: Ensure that the search does not